## TARGET PATENT (Patent B) — Prior art reference

**Label:** Prior1- A

**Independent Claim:**
A method for text-guided audio modification, the method comprising:
receiving source audio data;
applying noise reduction processing to the source audio data to produce cleaned audio;
extracting audio feature embeddings from the cleaned audio;
receiving a textual description specifying target voice attributes;
computing text feature embeddings from the textual description;
aligning the audio feature embeddings with the text feature embeddings to determine transformation parameters;
transforming the cleaned audio according to the transformation parameters to generate output audio having the target voice attributes; and
providing the output audio for playback.

**Specification Support:**
Noise Reduction: "The system applies spectral subtraction and Wiener filtering to remove background noise, environmental interference, and signal artifacts from the input audio waveform, producing a cleaned audio signal with improved signal-to-noise ratio."
Audio Embedding Generation: "Audio feature embeddings are extracted using a pre-trained audio encoder network (e.g., wav2vec, AudioCLIP) that processes the cleaned audio in overlapping windows and outputs 512-dimensional embedding vectors capturing phonetic, prosodic, and spectral characteristics."
Text Processing: "The textual description (e.g., 'make voice deeper and add British accent') is processed by a natural language understanding module that parses the attributes and generates corresponding text embeddings using a transformer-based language model (e.g., BERT, RoBERTa)."
Correlation/Alignment: "A cross-modal attention mechanism computes alignment scores between audio and text embedding spaces, identifying which audio features should be modified to match the text-described characteristics. The alignment produces transformation parameters specifying pitch shifts, formant adjustments, prosody modifications, and spectral envelope changes."
Audio Modification: "A neural vocoder (e.g., WaveNet, HiFi-GAN) applies the transformation parameters to the cleaned audio, synthesizing modified audio that exhibits the target voice attributes while preserving speaker identity and linguistic content."

