## TARGET PATENT (Patent B) — Prior art reference

**Label:** pa-antici

**Independent Claim:**
A computer-implemented method comprising:
obtaining a start image depicting an initial visual state;
obtaining an end image depicting a final visual state;
analyzing the start image using a neural network to identify objects and visual characteristics in the initial visual state;
analyzing the end image using a neural network to identify objects and visual characteristics in the final visual state;
calculating changes between the initial visual state and the final visual state;
generating, using a deep learning-based image generation model, multiple intermediate frames representing gradual transitions from the initial visual state to the final visual state;
assembling the start image, the multiple intermediate frames, and the end image into a frame sequence; and
outputting an animated video comprising the frame sequence.

**Specification Support:**
The present invention relates to generating smooth animated transitions between two input images. The system receives a first input image showing a scene at time T1 and a second input image showing the same scene at time T2. A convolutional neural network analyzes both images to extract feature representations and identify objects, movements, and transformations between the two states.
The system then employs a generative adversarial network (GAN) trained on video data to synthesize intermediate frames. The GAN takes the feature embeddings from both input images and generates N intermediate frames that smoothly interpolate between the two states. The interpolation is context-aware, ensuring that objects move naturally and visual coherence is maintained throughout the transition.
Finally, the system concatenates the first input image, all N intermediate frames, and the second input image into a video file format (e.g., MP4, GIF) with a specified frame rate (e.g., 24 fps). This creates a short animated clip showing the transformation from the first state to the second state.

