source_patent.independent_claim:
A method implemented by one or more processors, the method comprising:
receiving a code-mixed sentence comprising three or more languages;
receiving a target language specification, wherein the target language is different from each of the three or more languages;
detecting the three or more languages present in the code-mixed sentence;
determining, for each of the three or more languages, a semantic weight associated with that language in the code-mixed sentence;
identifying a dominant language from among the three or more languages based on the semantic weight, wherein the dominant language has a highest semantic weight;
generating an intermediate translation by translating the code-mixed sentence into the dominant language;
generating an initial target language translation by translating the intermediate translation from the dominant language to the target language;
processing the initial target language translation using an artificial intelligence (AI) verifier model, wherein the AI verifier model compares the initial target language translation against the code-mixed sentence;
receiving verification feedback from the AI verifier model;
responsive to the verification feedback indicating a verification failure, iteratively refining the target language translation by generating a revised target language translation based on the verification feedback until the verification feedback indicates a verification success; and
responsive to the verification feedback indicating a verification success, outputting a final target language translation.

