target_patent.independent_claim:
A computer-implemented method for translating multilingual text, comprising:
receiving an input sentence containing a mixture of three or more distinct languages;
identifying each of the three or more languages present in the input sentence using language detection;
computing a semantic importance score for each identified language based on semantic contribution to overall meaning;
selecting a pivot language from the identified languages, wherein the pivot language has the highest semantic importance score;
performing a first translation operation to convert the multilingual input sentence into the pivot language, producing a pivot language output;
performing a second translation operation to convert the pivot language output into a user-designated target language, producing a target language output;
submitting the target language output to an automated verification module comprising a neural network model;
the automated verification module analyzing semantic consistency between the target language output and the multilingual input sentence;
the automated verification module generating a quality assessment signal;
when the quality assessment signal indicates inadequate translation quality, transmitting correction signals to the translation operations to regenerate the target language output;
repeating the translation and verification operations iteratively until the quality assessment signal indicates adequate translation quality; and
outputting the target language output as a final translation when adequate translation quality is achieved.

