A method for providing task assistance using augmented reality glasses, the method comprising:
receiving, at augmented reality glasses, a voice command from a user indicating a repair task to be performed on a mechanical device;
activating a camera sensor, a microphone sensor, and a motion sensor of the augmented reality glasses;
capturing image data from the camera sensor showing the mechanical device;
capturing audio data from the microphone sensor detecting ambient sounds;
capturing motion data from the motion sensor detecting user head movements;
analyzing the image data using computer vision to identify components of the mechanical device;
combining the image data, the audio data, and the motion data to determine a current state of the repair task;
determining that information is needed about which component the user intends to remove;
generating a clarifying question: "Do you want to remove the left bolt or the right bolt?";
displaying, on a transparent display of the augmented reality glasses, an arrow mark pointing to the left bolt and an arrow mark pointing to the right bolt;
displaying the clarifying question as text overlaid on the user's field of view;
detecting the user's verbal response through the microphone sensor;
updating the current state of the repair task based on the verbal response; and
generating a next assistance prompt based on the updated current state.

