## TARGET PATENT (Patent B) — Prior art reference

**Label:** pa-implici

**Independent Claim:**
A method for interactive guidance in a head-mounted display system, the method comprising:
receiving a user goal statement through a voice interface of a head-mounted display;
activating environmental sensing capabilities including optical sensors, acoustic sensors, and orientation sensors;
analyzing data from the optical sensors to recognize objects in a user's environment;
processing data from the acoustic sensors to detect environmental conditions;
utilizing data from the orientation sensors to determine user attention direction;
synthesizing the data from multiple sensing modalities to build a contextual model of the user's situation;
determining, based on the contextual model and the user goal, what additional information would facilitate goal completion;
formulating inquiries to obtain the additional information, wherein the inquiries address uncertainty in user intention, task progress confirmation, potential hazards, or state of environmental elements;
presenting graphical indicators in the head-mounted display to highlight relevant portions of the user's visual field; and
presenting textual content in the head-mounted display conveying the formulated inquiries.

**Specification Support:**
The specification describes a "smart coaching system" for a head-mounted display worn during cooking. The user says "Help me make pasta carbonara." The system activates its "perceptual array" including cameras (optical sensors), microphones (acoustic sensors), and "spatial trackers" (orientation sensors).
The cameras recognize ingredients on the counter, the microphones detect sizzling sounds from the stove, and the spatial trackers determine which direction the user is facing. The system builds a "situational awareness model" by "integrating multiple sensor streams" to understand the cooking context.
The specification states the system "identifies knowledge gaps that could impede task execution" and "generates queries to resolve ambiguities." Examples include asking whether the user wants to use guanciale or pancetta (intention), whether water is boiling yet (progress), whether the heat is too high based on smoke detection (hazards), or whether eggs are at room temperature (state).
The system uses "visual overlays" including "directional pointers" (arrows) and "text annotations" displayed in the user's field of view. While the specification doesn't explicitly use the exact phrase "multimodal sensor fusion" or "arrow marks," it describes the same functional approach of combining vision, audio, and motion data to generate contextual questions with visual hints.

target_patent.independent_claim:
A computer-implemented method comprising:
receiving a content generation request from a user;
generating initial content using a generative AI model based on the content generation request;
evaluating the initial content using a trained classification model configured to detect artificial-appearing characteristics in machine-generated content, wherein the classification model is trained on human annotations distinguishing between human-created content and machine-generated content perceived as artificial;
determining a slop score indicating a degree to which the initial content exhibits artificial-appearing characteristics;
when the slop score exceeds a quality threshold:

identifying specific artificial patterns in the initial content;
generating corrective guidance describing modifications to reduce artificial-appearing characteristics; and
regenerating content using the generative AI model based on the content generation request and the corrective guidance;

when the slop score does not exceed the quality threshold, selecting the initial content as final content; and
transmitting the final content to the user.

A method for improving machine-generated content quality, comprising:
receiving a user query and generating a first response using a language generation model;
computing a quality metric for the first response using a learned quality assessment model, wherein the quality assessment model is trained to predict user satisfaction scores;
when the quality metric falls below an acceptability threshold:

analyzing the first response to identify quality deficiencies; and
generating a refined response using the language generation model with modified generation parameters based on the identified quality deficiencies;

outputting either the first response or the refined response based on the quality metric.

source_patent.independent_claim:
A method implemented by one or more processors, the method comprising:
receiving a user input and generating a first AI-generated output based on the user input;
determining, using an AI slop evaluator model, whether the first AI-generated output exhibits AI slop characteristics;
responsive to determining that the first AI-generated output exhibits AI slop characteristics, generating a second AI-generated output based on improvement feedback; and
causing a final output to be rendered, wherein the final output comprises the second AI-generated output when AI slop characteristics are detected, or the first AI-generated output when AI slop characteristics are not detected.

